# Vendored/upstream code excluded from coverage measurement.
# pladdrr's coverage should reflect pladdrr-authored code (R/ + the thin
# C++ wrappers in src/*.cpp and src/modules/), not the ~2.3M lines of
# vendored Praat DSP core or the bundled third-party FFT libraries.
src/praat.github.io
src/pffft
src/pocketfft

# Individually-confirmed fully-dead files (0.00%-or-near-0% baseline coverage,
# zero external callers). `// nocov start`/`// nocov end` markers do NOT work
# in C++ files under covr's default exclude-region regex (it requires a
# literal `#`, R-comment style, and never matches `//`) — this file-level
# .covrignore entry is the actual, working exclusion mechanism.
src/uiform_libmode.cpp
src/formantpath_simd.cpp
src/graphics_stubs_comprehensive.cpp
src/pitch_simd_bridge.cpp
src/uiform_stubs.cpp
# Legacy dead helpers: praat_error_to_r/throw_praat_error (unused by any R
# code; praat_error_to_r is an Rcpp::export but absent from NAMESPACE) and
# validate_*_object for the long-removed praat_sound/praat_pitch S3 classes
# (0 external callers). Whole-file exclusion is the only working mechanism.
src/utils.cpp
